{
  "description": "Combination rules applied to whole stacks. 'when' keys: frontend, backend, database, hosting, backend_kind, hosting_kind, hosting_provider (all listed keys must match). 'not' excludes matches. 'input' filters on project inputs ('skills_any': applies unless the team lists skills and none of these; 'skills_none': does not apply when the team lists any of these). delta is added to the stack score (in layer points: the stack score is (sum of the four layer scores + sum of deltas) / 4).",
  "rules": [
    {
      "id": "nextjs_vercel",
      "kind": "synergy",
      "delta": 5,
      "when": {
        "frontend": [
          "nextjs"
        ],
        "hosting": [
          "vercel"
        ]
      },
      "note": "Vercel builds Next.js: ISR, image optimisation, middleware and preview deploys work with zero configuration.",
      "source": "https://nextjs.org/docs/app/building-your-application/deploying"
    },
    {
      "id": "meta_fw_frontend_paas",
      "kind": "synergy",
      "delta": 6,
      "when": {
        "frontend": [
          "nuxt",
          "sveltekit",
          "astro"
        ],
        "hosting_kind": [
          "frontend_paas"
        ]
      },
      "note": "Official adapters/presets deploy this framework to the CDN + functions platform with no server to manage.",
      "source": "https://svelte.dev/docs/kit/adapters"
    },
    {
      "id": "static_spa_frontend_paas",
      "kind": "synergy",
      "delta": 4,
      "when": {
        "frontend": [
          "react_spa"
        ],
        "hosting_kind": [
          "frontend_paas",
          "static_cdn"
        ]
      },
      "note": "Static build output is served directly from a global CDN.",
      "source": "https://vite.dev/guide/static-deploy"
    },
    {
      "id": "supabase_postgres",
      "kind": "synergy",
      "delta": 4,
      "when": {
        "backend": [
          "supabase"
        ],
        "database": [
          "postgres"
        ]
      },
      "note": "Supabase is a managed Postgres: auth, row-level security, storage and realtime come with the database.",
      "source": "https://supabase.com/docs/guides/database/overview"
    },
    {
      "id": "supabase_other_db",
      "kind": "conflict",
      "delta": -50,
      "when": {
        "backend": [
          "supabase"
        ]
      },
      "not": {
        "database": [
          "postgres",
          "timescaledb"
        ]
      },
      "note": "Supabase's value comes from its bundled Postgres; a different primary database removes most of its benefits.",
      "source": "https://supabase.com/docs"
    },
    {
      "id": "supabase_timescale",
      "kind": "caveat",
      "delta": -8,
      "when": {
        "backend": [
          "supabase"
        ],
        "database": [
          "timescaledb"
        ]
      },
      "note": "Supabase deprecated the TimescaleDB extension on Postgres 17 projects; use native partitioning or a separate Timescale service.",
      "source": "https://supabase.com/docs/guides/database/extensions"
    },
    {
      "id": "firebase_firestore",
      "kind": "synergy",
      "delta": 4,
      "when": {
        "backend": [
          "firebase"
        ],
        "database": [
          "firestore"
        ]
      },
      "note": "Firebase SDKs give Firestore realtime listeners, offline cache and security rules end-to-end.",
      "source": "https://firebase.google.com/docs/firestore"
    },
    {
      "id": "firebase_other_db",
      "kind": "conflict",
      "delta": -50,
      "when": {
        "backend": [
          "firebase"
        ]
      },
      "not": {
        "database": [
          "firestore"
        ]
      },
      "note": "Firebase is designed around Firestore/Realtime Database; pairing it with another primary DB needs a separate server tier.",
      "source": "https://firebase.google.com/docs"
    },
    {
      "id": "firestore_without_firebase_offgcp",
      "kind": "conflict",
      "delta": -12,
      "when": {
        "database": [
          "firestore"
        ]
      },
      "not": {
        "backend": [
          "firebase"
        ],
        "hosting_provider": [
          "gcp"
        ]
      },
      "note": "Firestore outside Google Cloud adds cross-cloud latency and egress costs.",
      "source": "https://cloud.google.com/firestore/docs/locations"
    },
    {
      "id": "dynamodb_off_aws",
      "kind": "conflict",
      "delta": -20,
      "when": {
        "database": [
          "dynamodb"
        ]
      },
      "not": {
        "hosting_provider": [
          "aws"
        ]
      },
      "note": "DynamoDB is AWS-only; calling it from another cloud adds latency, egress fees and IAM key management.",
      "source": "https://docs.aws.amazon.com/amazondynamodb/latest/developerguide/Introduction.html"
    },
    {
      "id": "dynamodb_lambda",
      "kind": "synergy",
      "delta": 8,
      "when": {
        "database": [
          "dynamodb"
        ],
        "hosting": [
          "aws_lambda"
        ]
      },
      "note": "DynamoDB uses HTTP, not long-lived connections, so Lambda concurrency cannot exhaust a connection pool.",
      "source": "https://docs.aws.amazon.com/lambda/latest/dg/with-ddb.html"
    },
    {
      "id": "lambda_rdbms_pooling",
      "kind": "caveat",
      "delta": -4,
      "when": {
        "hosting": [
          "aws_lambda"
        ],
        "database": [
          "postgres",
          "mysql",
          "timescaledb",
          "sqlserver"
        ]
      },
      "not": {
        "backend": [
          "supabase"
        ]
      },
      "note": "Each Lambda instance opens its own DB connection; put RDS Proxy (or PgBouncer/Neon pooler) in front to avoid connection exhaustion.",
      "source": "https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonRDS/latest/UserGuide/rds-proxy.html"
    },
    {
      "id": "frontend_paas_rdbms_pooling",
      "kind": "caveat",
      "delta": -2,
      "when": {
        "hosting_kind": [
          "frontend_paas"
        ],
        "database": [
          "postgres",
          "mysql",
          "sqlserver"
        ]
      },
      "not": {
        "backend": [
          "supabase"
        ]
      },
      "note": "Serverless functions need a pooled/HTTP driver (Neon serverless driver, Supabase pooler, PlanetScale) to avoid connection exhaustion.",
      "source": "https://neon.tech/docs/serverless/serverless-driver"
    },
    {
      "id": "faas_backend_on_faas_host",
      "kind": "synergy",
      "delta": 4,
      "when": {
        "backend": [
          "serverless_functions"
        ],
        "hosting": [
          "aws_lambda",
          "vercel",
          "netlify",
          "gcp_cloud_run",
          "azure_apps",
          "digitalocean",
          "cloudflare"
        ]
      },
      "note": "Functions deploy natively on this platform's function runtime.",
      "source": "https://vercel.com/docs/functions"
    },
    {
      "id": "faas_backend_no_faas_host",
      "kind": "conflict",
      "delta": -30,
      "when": {
        "backend": [
          "serverless_functions"
        ],
        "hosting": [
          "render",
          "railway",
          "flyio",
          "hetzner",
          "onprem_docker",
          "onprem_k8s",
          "aws_ecs",
          "aws_eks",
          "gcp_gke"
        ]
      },
      "note": "This host has no managed function runtime; you would need Knative/OpenFaaS or to rewrite as a server.",
      "source": "https://knative.dev/docs/"
    },
    {
      "id": "heavy_server_on_frontend_paas",
      "kind": "conflict",
      "delta": -24,
      "when": {
        "backend": [
          "spring_boot",
          "dotnet",
          "rails",
          "phoenix",
          "django",
          "laravel"
        ],
        "hosting_kind": [
          "frontend_paas"
        ]
      },
      "note": "Frontend platforms run code only as short-lived functions; this framework expects a long-running server. Host the API on a container/PaaS service instead.",
      "source": "https://vercel.com/docs/functions/runtimes"
    },
    {
      "id": "light_server_on_frontend_paas",
      "kind": "caveat",
      "delta": -10,
      "when": {
        "backend": [
          "express",
          "nestjs",
          "fastapi",
          "go"
        ],
        "hosting_kind": [
          "frontend_paas"
        ]
      },
      "note": "This framework can be adapted to serverless functions, but you lose in-memory state, background jobs and WebSockets.",
      "source": "https://vercel.com/docs/functions/runtimes"
    },
    {
      "id": "monolith_on_frontend_paas",
      "kind": "caveat",
      "delta": -10,
      "when": {
        "backend": [
          "express",
          "nestjs",
          "fastapi",
          "go",
          "spring_boot",
          "dotnet",
          "rails",
          "phoenix",
          "django",
          "laravel"
        ],
        "hosting_kind": [
          "frontend_paas"
        ]
      },
      "input": {
        "architecture": [
          "monolith"
        ]
      },
      "note": "You asked for one deployable monolith; a frontend platform runs pages and short functions, not a long-running server process, so the server would have to be split off or rewritten as functions.",
      "source": "https://vercel.com/docs/functions/runtimes"
    },
    {
      "id": "heavy_server_on_lambda",
      "kind": "caveat",
      "delta": -14,
      "when": {
        "backend": [
          "spring_boot",
          "dotnet",
          "rails",
          "phoenix",
          "django",
          "laravel"
        ],
        "hosting": [
          "aws_lambda"
        ]
      },
      "note": "Large frameworks suffer cold starts on Lambda (SnapStart helps Java); containers on ECS/Cloud Run fit better.",
      "source": "https://docs.aws.amazon.com/lambda/latest/dg/snapstart.html"
    },
    {
      "id": "light_server_on_lambda",
      "kind": "caveat",
      "delta": -4,
      "when": {
        "backend": [
          "express",
          "nestjs",
          "fastapi",
          "go"
        ],
        "hosting": [
          "aws_lambda"
        ]
      },
      "note": "Runs via an adapter (Lambda Web Adapter / Mangum); keep handlers stateless.",
      "source": "https://github.com/awslabs/aws-lambda-web-adapter"
    },
    {
      "id": "realtime_on_functions",
      "kind": "conflict",
      "delta": -20,
      "when": {
        "hosting": [
          "netlify",
          "aws_lambda"
        ]
      },
      "not": {
        "backend": [
          "supabase",
          "firebase"
        ]
      },
      "input": {
        "realtime": [
          "core"
        ]
      },
      "note": "No persistent WebSocket connections on this platform; you would need a managed realtime service (Ably, Pusher, API Gateway WebSockets).",
      "source": "https://docs.aws.amazon.com/lambda/latest/dg/lambda-runtime-environment.html"
    },
    {
      "id": "realtime_vercel_beta",
      "kind": "caveat",
      "delta": -6,
      "when": {
        "hosting": [
          "vercel"
        ]
      },
      "not": {
        "backend": [
          "supabase",
          "firebase"
        ]
      },
      "input": {
        "realtime": [
          "core"
        ]
      },
      "note": "Vercel Functions serve WebSockets in public beta: each connection pins to one instance, so broadcasting to many users needs a shared pub/sub (e.g. Redis) and reconnect handling.",
      "source": "https://vercel.com/kb/guide/do-vercel-serverless-functions-support-websocket-connections"
    },
    {
      "id": "many_connections_on_functions",
      "kind": "conflict",
      "delta": -12,
      "when": {
        "hosting": [
          "vercel",
          "netlify",
          "aws_lambda"
        ]
      },
      "not": {
        "backend": [
          "supabase",
          "firebase"
        ]
      },
      "input": {
        "realtime": [
          "some",
          "core"
        ],
        "concurrent_min": 1000
      },
      "note": "Thousands of users connected at once need processes that keep their connections open. Request-scoped functions either cannot hold a WebSocket (Lambda behind a function URL, Netlify) or hold each one as a running function pinned to one instance (Vercel beta), so broadcasting to all of them needs a separate pub/sub or realtime service.",
      "source": "https://vercel.com/kb/guide/do-vercel-serverless-functions-support-websocket-connections"
    },
    {
